Chapter: Hart

 HART (Highway Addressable Remote Transducer), the field-instrument
 protocol that carries digital messages over the 4-20 mA analog current
 loops of process plants -- transmitters, valve positioners, and
 controllers in oil and gas, chemical, and water treatment. A frame is
 a run of 0xFF preamble octets, a delimiter announcing the frame and
 address form, an address (a one-octet polling address or a five-octet
 unique device identifier), a command, a byte count, the data, and a
 one-octet longitudinal parity (XOR) checksum computed from the
 delimiter through the last data octet. Each builder returns a
 List Integer.

Section: Delimiters

 The delimiter's low bits name the frame type (STX from a master, ACK
 from a field device); its high bit selects the short polling address
 or the long unique-identifier address form.

  hart-delim-stx-short : Integer = #02
  hart-delim-ack-short : Integer = #06
  hart-delim-stx-long : Integer = #82
  hart-delim-ack-long : Integer = #86

Section: Preamble and Checksum

  hart-preamble : Integer -> List Integer
  hart-preamble (n) = hart-preamble-loop n []

  hart-preamble-loop : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  hart-preamble-loop (n) (acc) =
   if n <= 0 then acc else hart-preamble-loop (n - 1) (list-push acc #FF)

  hart-checksum : List Integer -> Integer
  hart-checksum (bytes) = hart-xor-loop bytes 0 (list-length bytes) 0

  hart-xor-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  hart-xor-loop (bytes) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else hart-xor-loop bytes (i + 1) len (bit-xor acc (list-at bytes i))

Section: Addressing

 A short address packs a four-bit polling address with a master bit
 (the primary master sets it) and a burst-mode bit. A long address is
 the device's five-octet unique identifier.

  hart-short-address : Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  hart-short-address (poll-addr) (master) =
   bit-or (if master then #80 else 0) (bit-and poll-addr #0F)

Section: Commands

  hart-cmd-read-unique-id : Integer = 0
  hart-cmd-read-pv : Integer = 1
  hart-cmd-read-current-and-pv : Integer = 2
  hart-cmd-read-dynamic-vars : Integer = 3
  hart-cmd-set-polling-address : Integer = 6

Section: Frames

 Five preamble octets precede the message body; the checksum covers the
 body from the delimiter through the data.

  hart-short-frame : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  hart-short-frame (address) (command) (data) =
   let core = [hart-delim-stx-short, address, command, list-length data] & data
   in hart-preamble 5 & core & [hart-checksum core]

  hart-long-frame : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  hart-long-frame (uid) (command) (data) =
   let core = [hart-delim-stx-long] & uid & [command, list-length data] & data
   in hart-preamble 5 & core & [hart-checksum core]
